ities than ever  and because of rising yields because of  inflation because of just say you know a  global pandemic that that tank's  productivity what happens uh well the  earnings side of your balance sheet goes  down one person's earnings or one  person's spending is another person's  income and it's reinforcing on the  downside and all of a sudden now you  have a huge asset liability mismatch but  then the bad side and so what happens is  well you have an asset liability  mismatch you sell what you can to pay  down your liabilities and it's just a  cascading event where everything kind of  the house of cards falls down and so  we're not there yet i mean i'm not  calling for the end of the world  but this is why these credit you know  expansion and credit contractions this  is how they work um fiat money is  destroyed through debt debt uh default  or repayment and so when you have kind  of these mass default events these mass  insolvencies right now we're kind of in  the liquidity risk uh environment what  that eventually leads to uh if central  banks and governments don't kind of step  in and and help uh you know remonetize a  lot of this debt and inflate people's  balance sheets is what happens is that  that liquidity risk turns into solvency  risk and that's when kind of it turns  into actually systematic risk for the  fiat itself hey you did you like this  video great we make five of them a day  and post them here on this channel make  sure you subscribe like the video and  see you next time

